### 3. $\lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin x}{x}$.

1. Al evaluar directamente en $x=0$, obtenemos $\frac{\sin(0)}{0} = \frac{0}{0}$, una forma indeterminada.

2. Utilizamos la Regla de L'Hôpital, derivando el numerador y el denominador de manera independiente con respecto a $x$.
   * Derivada del numerador: $\frac{d}{dx}(\sin x) = \cos x$
   * Derivada del denominador: $\frac{d}{dx}(x) = 1$
3. Evaluamos el nuevo límite:

   $$ \lim_{x\to0} \frac{\cos x}{1} = \cos(0) = 1 $$

$$ \lim_{x\to0}\frac{\sin x}{x} = 1 $$

```{r}
#| echo: false
#| message: false
#| warning: false

x_vals3 <- seq(-4*pi, 4*pi, length.out = 500)
x_vals3 <- x_vals3[abs(x_vals3) > 0.05] 
df_sinc <- data.frame(x = round(x_vals3, 2), y = round(sin(x_vals3)/x_vals3, 4))

hchart(df_sinc, "line", hcaes(x = x, y = y), color = "#8E44AD", name = "sin(x)/x") %>%
  hc_add_series(
    data = data.frame(x = 0, y = 1), type = "scatter", 
    hcaes(x = x, y = y), name = "Límite L", color = "#E67E22",
    marker = list(radius = 6, fillColor = "white", lineWidth = 2, lineColor = "#E67E22")
  ) %>%
  hc_yAxis(title = list(text = "f(x)")) %>%
  hc_xAxis(title = list(text = "x"), crosshair = TRUE) %>%
  hc_tooltip(headerFormat = "", pointFormat = "<b>x:</b> {point.x} <br> <b>f(x):</b> {point.y}")
```

